DRAFT — NOT ADOPTED. See ./README.md before using this file.

This file presents TWO MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE OPTIONS. The owner must choose one, have it
reviewed by counsel, and only then place the chosen text at the repository root as /LICENSE.

Background (see ../06-compliance.md §1.1-1.2):
  - README.md currently states "MIT" but NO LICENSE FILE EXISTS. No licence has been
    effectively granted.
  - The MIT licence expressly permits anyone to "sublicense, and/or sell copies of the
    Software". It is therefore incompatible with selling this as a commercial product:
    a customer or competitor could lawfully resell it, or strip the licence-key check.
  - Before adopting EITHER option, Legal Questions 1 and 2 must be answered: whether the
    owner can relicense given prior releases claiming MIT, and whether any third-party
    contributions exist that would require a contributor licence agreement.

================================================================================
OPTION A — PROPRIETARY END-USER LICENCE AGREEMENT  (RECOMMENDED)
================================================================================

Recommended because it is the only option consistent with the self-hosted commercial model
recommended in ../../gtm/07-marketplace-readiness.md §1. Source may still be published for
transparency ("source-available"); this licence does not grant the right to redistribute,
resell, or remove licensing controls.

